      "blurb": "Volus trade operative, non-combat encounter or hostile negotiator",
      "publicNotes": "<p>Volus merchants are not soldiers and do not pretend to be. They are, however, extraordinarily good at creating situations where combat is disadvantageous-through economic leverage, information brokerage, and the simple fact that killing a volus merchant often triggers consequences that outlast the satisfaction of the act. When forced into direct confrontation, they are relying entirely on whatever security they've hired.</p><p><strong>Market Instinct:</strong> Can determine item value within 10%. +2 circ. vs. trade deception; +2 circ. Sense Motive vs. value misrepresentation.</p><p><strong>Hired Security:</strong> Typically accompanied by 1d4 mercenaries of appropriate level.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 25 Shield HP. Recharges 7 HP per turn.</p>",
